The utility is a very simple DHCP client which can be used to ap‐
ply  networking  configuration on one interface in a rump kernel.
Unlike full DHCP clients, does not store leases or renew  expired
leases.  The reason for this is the typical transient nature of a
rump  kernel.   Additionally, does not save DNS resolver informa‐
tion.  After having successfully  configured  networking,  prints
out the networking configuration and lease time and exits.  Since
uses to send and receive raw network packets, the server must in‐
clude support for bpf and vfs (for opening Otherwise, the follow‐
ing diagnostic message is printed: rump.dhcpclient: bpf: Function
not implemented There is no easy way to release a lease.
